{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-017", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Women-led Vietnamese firms urged to strengthen sustainable exports", "content": "Vietnam has urged women-owned and gender-responsive enterprises to strengthen traceability, transparency and sustainable practices as global markets tighten supply-chain requirements. \nOfficials said tariff preferences under FTAs are no longer sufficient, with exporters required to meet standards covering sustainability, labour, environmental compliance, product safety and corporate responsibility.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/women-led-vietnamese-firms-urged-to-strengthen-sustainable-exports-313029-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-018", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["increase", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's 36% Cambodia trade surge sets up a new textile opportunity", "content": "India-Cambodia trade rose more than 36 per cent to $406.78 million in 2025-26, while April-June 2026 trade increased 63.25 per cent YoY.\nCambodia is India's eighth-largest ASEAN partner and accounts for just 0.31 per cent of India-ASEAN trade.\nBoth countries face a 10 per cent US forced-labour duty, weakening the case for shifting apparel production to Cambodia.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-36-cambodia-trade-surge-sets-up-a-new-textile-opportunity-313032-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-019", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["increase", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India cotton yarn notices mixed trend, overseas demand better", "content": "Ludhiana cotton yarn prices rose by ₹2 per kg on strong export orders, while Delhi stayed stable amid weak domestic buying.\nHigher yarn costs squeezed weaving margins as fabric and garment buyers resisted price increases.\nPanipat recycled yarn held steady ahead of expected festive demand, while North India cotton prices steadied after Wednesday’s surge.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-cotton-yarn-notices-mixed-trend-overseas-demand-better-313021-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-020", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "88.35¢ cotton: Can the new US quota shift Asian sourcing?", "content": "US plans a cotton-linked TRQ for Bangladesh, Cambodia, Indonesia and Malaysia, replacing the 10 per cent Section 301 duty with duty-free entry if garments use US cotton.\nThe enabling rule and Customs quota bulletin are unpublished, so covered apparel keeps paying the full 10 per cent duty.\nUS cotton is near a two-year high, with ICE December cotton at 88.35 cents/lb and Cotlook A at 98.90 cents.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/88-35-cotton-can-the-new-us-quota-shift-asian-sourcing--313012-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-021", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India plans 100 ships to cut $75 billion foreign freight bill", "content": "India’s National Shipping Board has backed a five-pillar plan to add 100 vessels over five years and reduce reliance on foreign shipping lines.\nThe plan matters to textile and apparel exporters because India pays about $75 billion a year in freight to foreign carriers.\nPanels cited a 16-20 per cent Indian-flag cost gap and called for fiscal, cargo, financing and regulatory reforms.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-plans-100-ships-to-cut-75-billion-foreign-freight-bill-313011-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-022", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Surat weavers cut production as crude, polyester yarn prices surge", "content": "Surat’s Unn weaving units will shut two days a week as polyester yarn, PTA and MEG costs squeeze power loom margins. \nOver 800 factories with around 30,000 looms make mainly polyester grey fabric, but buyers are resisting higher rates. \nSGCCI seeks an extension of temporary customs duty relief on PTA and MEG as volatile crude prices keep the value chain under pressure. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/surat-weavers-cut-production-as-crude-polyester-yarn-prices-surge-313010-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-023", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton bounces back on weather concerns, commodity rise", "content": "ICE cotton futures recovered after Tuesday’s correction, with the December 2026 contract settling at a contract high of 89.14 cents, up 0.80 cent. \nVolume was 40,085 contracts, light versus the 2026 average of 70,981, while 2028 contracts fell for a fourth session. \nHot, dry weather in key US growing regions and lower certified stocks supported cotton despite a 0.2 per cent stronger dollar. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-bounces-back-on-weather-concerns-commodity-rise-313008-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-024", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam urges Chinese investors to deepen local supply-chain links", "content": "Vietnamese Prime Minister Lê Minh Hưng has urged Chinese investors to focus on higher-quality projects, technology transfer, localisation and stronger links with Vietnamese businesses. \nBilateral trade reached around $184.3 billion in the first seven months, up 35.1 per cent year on year, while Chinese investors registered nearly $3.7 billion in investment capital.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-urges-chinese-investors-to-deepen-local-supply-chain-links-313006-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-27-025", "date": "2026-08-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "China's 19% Japan apparel decline could open India a $31bn market", "content": "India ships garments to Japan duty-free since 2011, but still accounts for under 2 per cent of the market.\nJapan’s apparel imports from China fell for four straight years to $11.23 billion in 2024, over 19 per cent below 2021.\nChina’s share falls below half in 2025 as Vietnam and Bangladesh gain from China-plus-one sourcing by buyers and manufacturers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/china-s-19-japan-apparel-decline-could-open-india-a-31bn-market-313034-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
